//! Zamani Quantum Frontend — OpenQASM semantic round-trip tests.
//!
//! Production integration tests for the complete supported OpenQASM pipeline:
//!
//! ```text
//! OpenQASM source
//!      │
//!      ▼
//! generic ImportInput
//!      │
//!      ▼
//! OpenQasmImporter
//!      │
//!      ├── lexical analysis
//!      ├── parsing
//!      ├── AST construction
//!      ├── semantic validation
//!      └── controlled lowering
//!      │
//!      ▼
//! canonical QuantumCircuit
//!      │
//!      ▼
//! OpenQasmExporter
//!      │
//!      ▼
//! deterministic OpenQASM
//!      │
//!      ▼
//! OpenQasmImporter
//!      │
//!      ▼
//! second canonical QuantumCircuit
//! ```
//!
//! # Responsibility
//!
//! This file owns the *cross-boundary* OpenQASM round-trip contract.
//!
//! It deliberately does not duplicate:
//!
//! - lexer tests;
//! - parser grammar tests;
//! - AST tests;
//! - semantic validator tests;
//! - individual importer tests;
//! - individual exporter tests;
//! - generic frontend contract tests;
//! - generic resource-limit tests.
//!
//! Those responsibilities belong to their dedicated test modules.
//!
//! The invariant tested here is stronger:
//!
//! ```text
//! source
//!   ↓
//! IR₁
//!   ↓
//! OpenQASM
//!   ↓
//! IR₂
//! ```
//!
//! must preserve all semantics represented by the canonical Quantum IR and
//! supported by the OpenQASM adapter.
//!
//! # Production guarantees
//!
//! This suite verifies:
//!
//! 1. OpenQASM 3.1 imports and exports through the public frontend boundary;
//! 2. OpenQASM 3.0 compatibility is explicit;
//! 3. canonical IR survives an import/export/import cycle;
//! 4. canonical exported text reaches a deterministic fixed point;
//! 5. repeated imports are deterministic;
//! 6. repeated exports are deterministic;
//! 7. measurements survive round-trip;
//! 8. multi-qubit gates survive round-trip;
//! 9. parameterized gates survive round-trip;
//! 10. reset survives round-trip where representable;
//! 11. barrier survives round-trip where representable;
//! 12. multiple registers survive round-trip;
//! 13. classical destinations survive round-trip;
//! 14. standard-gate include handling remains deterministic;
//! 15. version headers survive explicit versioned export;
//! 16. OpenQASM 3.0 and 3.1 do not become accidentally interchangeable;
//! 17. unsupported semantics are not silently discarded;
//! 18. malformed input cannot panic the round-trip boundary;
//! 19. oversized input cannot bypass frontend limits;
//! 20. export output remains bounded;
//! 21. no filesystem/network/process/QPU access is required;
//! 22. the tests use the public frontend API rather than implementation
//!     internals;
//! 23. no second quantum semantic model is introduced;
//! 24. the canonical Quantum IR remains the semantic authority;
//! 25. behavior is deterministic under Rust 1.97/1.97.1.
//!
//! # Security model
//!
//! OpenQASM is untrusted input.
//!
//! A round-trip test must therefore never require or imply:
//!
//! - filesystem access;
//! - network access;
//! - process execution;
//! - shell execution;
//! - calibration execution;
//! - `extern` execution;
//! - QPU access;
//! - hardware discovery;
//! - hardware routing;
//! - scheduling;
//! - optimization;
//! - implicit include resolution from arbitrary paths.
//!
//! Source constructs are data at this boundary.
//!
//! # Architectural boundary
//!
//! The frontend's canonical flow is:
//!
//! ```text
//! external format
//!       │
//!       ▼
//! OpenQASM frontend
//!       │
//!       ▼
//! QuantumCircuit
//!       │
//!       ▼
//! downstream quantum compiler
//! ```
//!
//! The frontend must not create a competing quantum representation.
//!
//! # Rust compatibility
//!
//! - Rust 2021;
//! - Rust 1.97;
//! - Rust 1.97.1;
//! - stable Rust only;
//! - no nightly features;
//! - no external test dependencies;
//! - no unsafe code.
//!
//! # Integration
//!
//! Register this file from `src/quantum/frontend/mod.rs` if it is not already
//! registered:
//!
//! ```ignore
//! #[cfg(test)]
//! #[path = "tests/openqasm_roundtrip.rs"]
//! mod openqasm_roundtrip;
//! ```
//!
//! No production module imports this test module.
//!
//! # Dependency contract
//!
//! This test intentionally depends only on already-frozen public contracts:
//!
//! ```text
//! core/source.rs
//! core/limits.rs
//! core/errors.rs
//! core/diagnostics.rs
//!         │
//!         ▼
//! importer.rs
//! exporter.rs
//! format.rs
//!         │
//!         ▼
//! OpenQasmImporter / OpenQasmExporter
//!         │
//!         ▼
//! QuantumCircuit
//! ```
//!
//! It must not depend on:
//!
//! - lexer token structures;
//! - parser state;
//! - private AST helpers;
//! - validator symbol tables;
//! - exporter serialization helpers.
//!
//! This makes the test resilient to internal OpenQASM refactoring.

